  "source": "synthetic demonstration atlas · not measured data",
  "note": "Whole-body passive stiffness in the form a myotonometry session export takes: dynamic stiffness in N/m per structure, with dispersion and repetition count where the device reports them. Values are synthetic but plausible (relaxed skeletal muscle roughly 150–350 N/m, dense fascia and retinacula far higher), arranged as the classic prolonged-seated-work pattern: elevated cervico-scapular and suboccipital stiffness, a stiff thoracolumbar junction, guarded hip flexors, and stiff plantar tissue. Three loader behaviours are exercised deliberately: FASCIA_DEEP_CERVICAL and ORGAN_DIAPHRAGM are aliases and resolve to their canonical structures; the PLANTAR and LEG region codes fan a floor value out to every structure whose centre lies in those regions without overriding the explicit entries above them; and MUSCLE_SOLEUS_L names a structure this model does not have, so it is reported as unresolved rather than silently dropped.",
